{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["And the sense of <b>and Pharaoh's princes saw her</b> is that when the Egyptians saw her, they said, \"This one is fitting for the great princes,\" and so they brought her to them. And they too were afraid for themselves to touch her, because on account of her great beauty they knew that the king would desire her very much. And they praised her among themselves, saying, \"She is fitting for the king\" — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 12:15). And this is the view of Onkelos (Onkelos on Genesis 12:15), who said, ושבחו יתה לות פרעה (\"and they praised her to Pharaoh\"). Alternatively, they praised her to the king himself, and he sent and took her."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:27:46.640701110Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}